# 06 · API and Data

## API Design Principles
- Design around stable business capabilities, not internal implementation details.
- Use explicit versioning/compatibility strategy for public interfaces.
- Prefer idempotent operations where retries are expected.

## Contracts and Schemas
- Define request/response/event schemas explicitly.
- Validate input and output against contracts.
- Document error formats and status semantics consistently.

## Data Modeling
- Model entities and relationships with clear ownership and lifecycle rules.
- Keep invariants enforceable at the right layer (app + storage constraints).
- Avoid duplication unless denormalization is deliberate and documented.

## Data Changes
- Use forward-compatible, reversible migration plans where possible.
- Backfill and migration jobs must be observable and resumable.
- Validate data integrity before and after large migrations.

## Reliability and Consistency
- Choose consistency model intentionally (strong/eventual) per workflow.
- Define conflict resolution strategy for concurrent updates.
- Implement retry and deduplication behavior for at-least-once delivery paths.

## Privacy and Retention
- Store only required data.
- Classify sensitive fields and protect accordingly.
- Apply retention/deletion policies and verify they execute correctly.
